# Default `mogwai serve --log-file` target; logs are runtime output, not source.
mogwai.log
# Default `mogwai serve --pid-file` target; the daemon PID lock, not source.
mogwai.pid
# `scripts/probe_warmup_window.py --log-file` target; runtime output.
scripts/probe-warmup.log
# `analysis/plot_tape.py` scratch: dumped tapes and the HTML charts built from
# them. Both regenerate from one command, neither is source.
/analysis/out/
# Regenerable Phase 0 intermediates; the durable artifact is fingerprint.json.
/analysis/char_*.json
/analysis/recon.json
# `select_windows.py features` cache, ~4 MB, derived from the vendor bar
# archives under the gitignored research/. Nobody without those archives can use
# it and anybody with them can rebuild it in one command, so it is not source.
# The Databento response cache beside it IS committed: it is 30 KB, it makes the
# priced baskets checkable without an API key, and it can hold no secret because
# only successful response bodies are ever written.
/analysis/cme_daily_features.json
# Per-month 1-minute bars, 126 MB, derived from the gitignored Binance archives
# under research/market-data. Nobody without those archives can use them and
# anybody with them rebuilds in one command. The DERIVED SUMMARIES beside them
# are committed and are the durable artifact: bar-scores-frozen.json is 8 KB,
# targets-frozen.json likewise, and analysis/preflight/ is 232 KB of per-month
# contract evidence that records why the 19-month span was confirmed.
/analysis/bars/
/analysis/targets/

# The buy-lock beside the committed job ledger, and the write-lock beside the
# committed response cache: kernel-held runtime state, empty, never content.
/analysis/databento-jobs.json.lock
/analysis/databento_cache.json.lock
